## Why does this work when not piped?

If yarg's `setBlocking` function isn't called until the error is thrown, I'm not sure why this works when `stdout`/`stderr` is not piped. My guess is Node.js actually calls `_handle.setBlocking(true)` behind the scenes.

https://github.com/nodejs/node/blob/ab89024ddc777ff888df0e239355f563e4cfa2a8/lib/tty.js

